[%title]: Aligned maths

Two rules:
$$$
a &= b + c
  &= d
$$$

A blank row is an empty row, as the post uses:
$$$
f(0) = x
g(0) = y

h(0) = z
$$$

Between rows with `&`, a blank row would be a short row, so it is written as `&` alone:
$$$
a &= b
&
c &= d
$$$

$$$
\underbrace{f(t)}_{\text{response}} &= \int_0^t g(s)\, ds % a comment
$$$
